+## G479 — 093-06: masked-alpha masks do not cover the union of both silhouettes
+
+The target mask follows the event-state silhouette. When corrupted alpha cuts pixels
+away, those pixels change outside the mask. The J1 masked-alpha PIE/staged readers
+therefore find more change in the surrounding ring than in the masked region, while
+onset/recovery edges remain 0 frames off. A measured nonzero event mask and correct
+timing do not certify completeness against the entire changed area. Ruling 093-05 E3
+records this as a known limitation, also listed in `client-readme.md`.
+
+Future item for the regular delivery line: mask the union of the pre-event and event
+silhouettes for silhouette-changing corruptions and gate mask completeness against
+the changed area. This is not natural-cause work and is not implemented by J2.
+
+## G480 — 093-06: request ownership includes the display generation and actual view
+
+A known scene/target is insufficient if a different local player, family, view state
+or display generation can supply the result. J2 freezes those identities before a
+request can dequeue and checks them again on the render thread and at publication.
+Viewport changes retire queued work and measurement baselines. Rejected readbacks
+already scheduled into RDG must remain alive until the GPU completes; then discard
+their bytes. A rejection cannot free a resource that a submitted GPU pass still uses.
+
+NotGameView has three different causes: the Game show flag, the game-thread view flag
+and a negative controller ID. Keep each counter and prove healthy capture on each
+fixture. Rejection totals count predicate checks, not frames; served masks include
+census and probe requests. Read `capture_ownership` in `run_summary.json`, not labels.
+
+The independent bench marker also needs the actual local-player projection. Building
+its position from FOV and viewport aspect clipped a reference cell on the Lyra fixture;
+all 360 upper frame barcodes and native event edges still matched. The failed evidence
+is retained in `_r936/legs/lyra_P_delayed`. The receipt-owned helper now deprojects its
+fixed normalized positions through the constrained view. The decoder and its contrast
+threshold are unchanged. This is a harness correction, not a product/view-gate exception.
+
+The later selected-viewport gate exposed a separate product disagreement. With the
+Lyra fixture's MaintainYFOV setting and a 942x869 selected viewport, the actual target
+projects entirely left of the image (X -79 to -21), but the label claims X 24 to 71.
+Ninety-six rows still say labelled/visible-positive with zero target pixels and no
+measured mask. All 360 pictures are from the correct view. The older product frustum
+reconstructs a horizontal FOV and predates J2. The job stops under D2 for review;
+changing the fixture framing must not silently conceal this label/picture failure.
+No product fix or relaxation of the gate was made. See `_r936/stop-review.json`.
