+## G481 — Camera FOV metadata is not the engine's projection geometry
+
+The retained 093-06 Lyra selected viewport exposes this directly: MaintainYFOV at
+942x869 put the target fully off the left edge while 96 rows claimed a visible
+box. The original framing is retained as PF-1, not silently replaced by a positive.
+At 1123x870, measured mask centres expose a projected-box scale of about 0.967.
+Null masks cannot supply the corresponding 942x869 mask estimate; report unavailable
+and keep the independent engine-corner evidence instead of inventing a reading.
+
+Use the resolved local player's engine projection, then freeze the actual serving
+view's unjittered matrices with the request. Refresh GT geometry after the camera
+update, before freezing bounds; replace it with serving geometry before any result
+membership calculation. Normalise against the same view rect copied by capture and
+map to the written picture size. Configured FOV remains a camera setting in labels,
+not an effective FOV inferred from a viewport aspect or an axis constraint.
+
+UE 5.1's `ULocalPlayer::GetViewPoint` is protected. Geometry comes from the public
+`GetProjectionData`; configured camera metadata comes from the public camera cache.
+Do not add a private engine header or engine edit to retrieve metadata.
+
+The PF-2/office estimator checks each axis separately and uses the worse deviation.
+A centre-near or clipped target, a missing mask, or fewer than 20 usable rows on an
+axis is insufficient evidence. The office reader counts null-mask labelled rows and
+continues its other checks. Machine view records cannot prove picture origin: the
+20-frame contact sheet stays local, and the owner appends the independent `g` count.
+Candidate implementation and qualification results are recorded separately in the
+093-07 journal; this note does not claim the unrun engine matrix has passed.
+
+PF-1 on the first 093-07 candidate demonstrates a separate admission gap: all 360
+rows correctly exclude the off-screen target, yet four targeted fires still apply.
+`TryFireSpecific` finds the named actor and calls ApplyAnomaly without an on-screen
+query. The four measured-zero annotation vetoes happen after apply and do not meet
+PF-1's no-fire/refusal requirement. The unchanged prediction fails; D2 stops the run.
+Do not claim that correcting the shared projector adds a check to callers that never
+consult it. The frozen failure and exact engine corners are in `_r937/stop-review.json`.
