+## G483 — Engine projection does not make the camera cache authoritative for FOV metadata
+
+`APlayerCameraManager::GetFOVAngle()` returns a positive LockedFOV before consulting
+the camera cache. The controller's `fov` command sets that lock. Reading
+`GetCameraCacheView().FOV` directly can therefore change the meaning of `fovDeg`
+even when the engine matrices produce correct boxes. Keep geometry on the engine
+projection and source the existing metadata key through GetFOVAngle. A control
+must use the observed cache value; never assume the unlocked FOV is 90.
+
+093-09 restores that accessor in AnomalyViewport.cpp without changing projection
+or visibility. PF-5 is the locked-value runtime proof in the frozen predictions.
+The admission proof is separate: the new Lyra PF-1 writes 360 frames, applies no
+fires and counts four off-screen refusals. Its retained 093-07 four-fire session
+still rejects, including through the generic apply receipt. Full qualification
+requires the remaining ordered gates; neither a build nor a source argument
+substitutes for those readings. See the 093-09 journal and `_r939` receipts.
+
+PF-5 now supplies the actual runtime values: requested=70, GetFOVAngle=70,
+camera-cache=90; every fovDeg label is 70 and both mask/box scale axes pass. The
+exact f9b9328 metadata expression would report the observed 90 and rejects the
+same locked-70 predicate. This proves the metadata repair, not full J2 qualification.
