+## G485 — The magenta pairing probe must be lit across its silhouette
+
+The permanent pairing reader measures bright-magenta pixels, not arbitrary dark
+geometry. Under the AA-off arbiter's disabled indirect lighting, the camera-facing
+probe face becomes black and the lit side pulls its centroid away from the full
+mask. Y1 classifies the 093-10 native100 leg as instrument precondition not met
+(probe unlit), with no pairing slip in evidence. Do not run this pairing reader
+at arbiter lighting. The arbiter's pixel-change purpose remains unchanged.
+093-11 freezes C1 without the three lighting overrides and C2 with only motion
+blur disabled; the control must establish the factor before adopting a recipe.
+The reader, 40 px tolerance and PREVIOUS = NEITHER = 0 predicate do not change.
+
+The 093-11 control establishes the factor: C1 with host lighting gives
+CURRENT52/PREVIOUS0/NEITHER0 and median probe coverage 68.47%; its shifted-mask
+copy rejects. The failed recipe gives 5.11% coverage and NEITHER56. C2 turns
+only motion blur off and still gives 5.15% coverage and NEITHER60. Adopt the
+amended recipe for all pairing legs; this does not authorize a different reader
+or a retry of PREVIOUS. No fixture material, light or product source changed.
+
+Later in the same job, Lyra native100 at amended lighting has 49 CURRENT and
+nine NEITHER despite 68.70% coverage. That cause is not established. The one
+remaining authorized recipe attempt, historic with all four arbiter overrides
+absent, passes 50 CURRENT/zero PREVIOUS/zero NEITHER and its shifted-mask control.
+Historic replaces amended for every pairing leg; both recipe attempts are now
+used. A lit probe is necessary for this reader, but this is not a claim that
+coverage alone establishes pairing correctness. Keep the actual gate and its
+can-fail, and do not infer a new tolerance from coverage.
+
+Historic native50 later pairs all 56 decidable samples CURRENT and rejects its
+shifted-mask control, while the frozen output-size check fails: 1280x992 actual
+against 640x496 expected. Serving-view diagnostics report TSR. Requested screen
+percentage and final picture dimensions are distinct measurements; a console
